<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cape Cod Bay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-cod">Cape Cod</a> Bay is a large bay of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> in Massachusetts, enclosed by the hooked peninsula of Cape Cod. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower">Mayflower</a> anchored at its tip, in Provincetown Harbor, in November 1620, and the Pilgrims then founded their settlement at Plymouth on its western shore in December. Its shores were home to the Wampanoag and other Native peoples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cape-cod-bay.jpg" alt="Cape Cod Bay" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NormanEinstein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cape_Cod_Bay_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
